desc:Emperor [Arcana synth] (GFX)
//tags: instrument synth bass sequencer step sequencer industrial ebm diode ladder distortion odd meter triplets arcana
//author: GardenFX
// by JGWizrad / Garden FX (GFX)
//
// Requires gfx-drift, gfx-output, gfx-ui, gfx-panel, gfx-instrument and gfx-voice (.jsfx-inc) in the same folder.
//
// THE EMPEROR (card IV of the GFX Arcana series): authority, structure, the fortress. A brutalist industrial bass
// sequencer synth - one monophonic voice, a stable square that can be clipped hard, an odd-harmonic sub, a noise
// source with its own lane, a diode ladder that can be driven into tuned self-oscillation, a sixteen-step grid that
// keeps rigid time (odd meters and triplets included), and a heavy distortion that leaves the sub clean.
//   OSC 1      a stable transistor square (band-limited pulse): LEVEL, PW (pulse width, 50 % = square) and
//              AUTHORITY - a hard clipper driven by up to 30 dB, level compensated: from a rounded square to a hard,
//              biased, buzzing edge (adds edge, not loudness). The grid's AUTHORITY lane adds to it step by step.
//   OSC 2      the SUB: an additive generator of odd harmonics an OCTAVE (-1 or -2) below OSC 1. HARMONICS: how many
//              odd partials (1 = a pure sine, up to 9: 1, 3, 5 .. 17), TILT: their slope, dark (triangle-like) to
//              bright (square-like), LEVEL. FATE wanders its tuning a little against OSC 1.
//   NOISE      white noise with its own short envelope: DECAY, COLOUR (a low band of steam to bright hats), LEVEL;
//              played only by the grid's NOISE lane. PRE sends it through THE WALL (it pings the filter), POST
//              around it.
//   THE WALL   a 4-pole diode ladder low-pass (zero-delay, stable at every setting): CUTOFF (black cap), RESONANCE,
//              WALL (the resonance drive: it overdrives the ladder's feedback and pushes it past self-oscillation;
//              the higher WALL, the more the cutoff locks to a harmonic of the note, so the scream is in tune),
//              KEY TRACK, ENV (the filter envelope's depth), DECAY (the filter envelope), ACCENT (how hard an
//              accented step hits: louder, a deeper and shorter filter sweep, more drive).
//   AMP        DECAY (while the step's gate is held) and RELEASE (after it); every attack is a short ramp, so a
//              step never clicks.
//   THE IRON GRID  sixteen steps, five lanes, edited on the CRT: PITCH (semitones -12 .. +24 from the key held -
//              MIDI transposes the pattern - or from ROOT when no key is held), the GATE / TIE / ACCENT flags (a
//              tied step does not strike again: it slides or steps on legato), SLEW (glide into that step, up to
//              GLIDE), AUTHORITY (added to the knob), CUTOFF (+/- 3 octaves on the Wall) and NOISE (a noise hit at
//              that level; 0 = none). Click or drag in a lane to draw, the wheel steps a value, a double-click
//              resets a step; click a flag to set or clear it (drag to paint). The lane keys pick the lane that
//              SHIFT (rotate), CLEAR and DECREE (a random pattern within reason) act on; ALL acts on every lane.
//              LENGTH 1 - 16 steps. The pattern is saved with the project and with every REAPER preset.
//   IRON FIST  the clock: 1/4, 1/8, 1/8T, 1/16, 1/16T, 1/32, or 5, 7, 9, 11 or 13 steps spread evenly across each
//              bar (the grid starts again every bar). SWING (straight divisions only; 0 by default - it is the
//              Emperor), GATE (the note length in a step), GLIDE, ROOT. RUN: the grid plays, locked to REAPER's
//              transport while it plays and free-running at the project tempo while it is stopped (to audition).
//              RUN off: the keys play the voice directly (mono, legato glide; velocity 110 and up accents).
//              TRANSPORT (lit by default): REAPER's play / record starts the grid and its stop stops it; RUN still
//              works by hand. Off, the grid ignores the transport.
//   DISTORTION a heavy industrial distortion with a SIDECHAIN crossover (Linkwitz-Riley, 40 - 400 Hz, yellow cap):
//              with CLEAN SUB lit everything below it bypasses the distortion clean and only the upper partials are
//              shredded. FUZZ (asymmetric, hard), RECTIFY (full-wave folded, an octave up), CRUSH (bits and rate);
//              DRIVE, TONE (dark .. bright), MIX.
//   DELAY      a tempo-synced echo after the distortion that returns into the output stage. Two sends, so either or
//              both can feed it: SYNTH (the Wall through the distortion, without the POST noise) and NOISE (what the
//              noise lane adds to the sound; PRE noise, which rings the Wall with the synth, is sent raw). TIME 1/16,
//              1/8T, 1/8, 1/8D, 1/4, 1/4D, 1/2 (a change crossfades, no click); FEEDBACK (a soft limiter in the loop:
//              stable at 100 %, where the echoes hold); TONE (the loop's low-pass); HPF SC (yellow cap, 40 - 600 Hz): a
//              high-pass on the way in and again in the loop, so the sub stays dry and only the upper part echoes;
//              RETURN (70 % = unity); DELAY IN / OUT; PING-PONG (left, then right).
//   LFO 1, 2   SHAPE (sine, triangle, saw, square, random steps), RATE (0.05 - 20 Hz, or with SYNC lit 4 bars .. 1/32,
//              triplets included, following REAPER's transport), DEPTH, a destination (drop-down): the Wall's CUTOFF
//              (+/- 3 octaves) or RESONANCE, the NOISE's LEVEL, COLOUR or DECAY. RETRIG restarts the wave every bar.
//              Glided, so a square or a random step never zippers.
//   ROOT and the MIDI channel are drop-downs (a click lists every value; the wheel steps).
//   FATE       the series' drift (0 - 100 %, 50 % = the standard amount): the pitch, the sub's tuning against OSC 1,
//              the Wall's cutoff and the distortion's tone wander slowly; every note lands a little differently.
//   VOLUME, SAT (the output soft clip is always on).
// MIDI: notes (transpose the grid, or play), pitch bend (+/- 2), CC120 / CC123 all notes off.

import gfx-drift.jsfx-inc
import gfx-output.jsfx-inc
import gfx-ui.jsfx-inc
import gfx-panel.jsfx-inc
import gfx-instrument.jsfx-inc
import gfx-voice.jsfx-inc

